5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"To make a logical choice, we should look at how previous projects actually performed. I'll start by checking the post-occupancy reviews and booking data.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with the need for data on usage. I want to see the booking data for rooms and the timetable records for rooms out of service.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A prudent approach. I am curious about why our timelines often slip, so I shall examine the delivery schedules and the site diaries.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to know if the money we plan actually covers the real costs! I'll check the tender records and the renewal reserves.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,You all focus on the buildings. I'm interested in the people. I'll look into the staffing posts and the bench technicians' manual routines.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
