30,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems our users are desperate for general-purpose space, while specialist rooms sit empty. We should prioritize projects that offer flexible, bookable access for everyone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,I've found that taking rooms out of service is incredibly expensive due to off-site hiring. We must consider the hidden costs of disruption to the timetable.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a pattern: ""comfort"" projects slip, and outdoor work is plagued by weather delays. We should perhaps favor essential upgrades over aesthetic ones.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"This is worrying! Mechanical costs are spiking, and we have no money set aside to replace old AV gear. We can't just trust the initial budget figures.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"While you discuss budgets, the staff are drowning. Specifically, technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks because the extraction equipment is obsolete.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that sounds like a critical failure. If the equipment is that bad, it's not just a comfort issue, but a functional one.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if outdoor work is so risky regarding the schedule, we might want to avoid extensive external renovations this year.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Victoria. A project that is ""nice to have"" but risks a year-long delay or weather setbacks is a logical gamble we shouldn't take.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, if we do a general space, we need to make sure the power and tech are budgeted for correctly, or we'll be broke again in five years.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. The current system is a drain on human resources. Fixing the ventilation isn't just about air; it's about reclaiming staff time.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,I'm torn between the need for general study space and the urgent need to support our staff. Both seem more vital than a niche media center.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The cost of off-site hiring makes me wary of any project that shuts down existing rooms for long periods. We need a plan with minimal disruption.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If we look at the data, an ""inspection-style"" necessity—like ventilation—is far more likely to be delivered on time than a ""comfort"" project.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the cost of mechanical plant upgrades since those prices are rising, but ignoring the renewal of equipment is also a disaster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Let's be rational. We have technicians doing manual labor that a machine should do. That is an inefficiency we can actually solve.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I see the logic. While students need space, the operational failure in the labs is a systemic issue that affects the whole faculty.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"If the ventilation upgrade is seen as a necessity rather than a luxury, it might avoid the ""comfort"" delay Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It is the most logically sound choice given the risks of weather and the history of delivery schedules.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"As long as we account for the price rise in mechanical lots, I can support the lab upgrade. It's better than a project that fails later.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we are in agreement. Let's prioritize the people and the infrastructure that supports them.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
